# CarbonLoom — Cursor & Assistant Rules

# Core Architectural Rule
- All emissions calculations, energy accounting, allocations, and financial figures MUST be computed using deterministic Python code. Never let an LLM do math.
- In documentation and UI, preliminary capabilities are tagged `[Designed]`, active features `[In progress]`, and tested CI-passing code `[Implemented]`.
- All simulated factory data must be explicitly flagged with `data_quality: "simulated"` and have a `SIMULATED DATA` watermark.

# Python & FastAPI Rules
- Use Pydantic v2 `BaseModel` with field types and strict validation.
- All database interactions must include `tenant_id` and respect PostgreSQL Row Level Security (RLS).
- In tests, ensure exact match against hand-verified formulas (0.00% error margin).

# Go MCP Gateway Rules
- Single Policy Enforcement Point (PEP) for all agent tool calls.
- Presidio redaction must run on all document payloads prior to LLM submission.
- Write tools MUST check for a single-use human approval token (`approval_token_id`).
- All tool calls must be appended to the SHA-256 hash-chained audit log.

# Frontend & UI (Hallmark + Unslop)
- Adhere strictly to Hallmark Floor rules: `:root` tokens for all colors/fonts, `overflow-x: clip`, focus-visible on all interactive elements.
- Adhere strictly to Unslop principles: 4px grid rhythm, single neutral ramp (graphite), no emoji icons (use Lucide 16-18px), tabular figures for numbers, no purple/blue glows or arbitrary gradients.
